General Summary of the position:
We have a requirement for a Senior Consultant for Economics to work with our multidisciplinary team to satisfy customer needs. Functions majorly involve providing consultancy services for our clients，often in the form of articles or reports. Candidates are expected to have knowledge and/or experience pertinent to this position. If you don’t fill all of the qualifications, you may still be considered depending on your level of experience.


Duties and Responsibilities:
Provide consulting services for customers;
Have the ability to independently complete research work and write articles or reports about economic and trade;
Analyze or explain the situation of economic development and economic and trade policies;
Evaluate various economic activities and study economic development trends;
Stay abreast of the direction of the economic circumstances, keep track of current events and policy issues;
Maintain confidentiality of clients
Interact with clients in a respectful and professional manner regardless of age, cultural background, ability, ethnicity, family status, gender identity, immigration status, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, socioeconomic status;
Conduct objective research that generates independent, high quality, and reproducible results. 

Qualifications:
Professionalism:
A Bachelor’s degree;
Familiar with international trade policies and regional cooperation events and trends;
A thorough awareness of specific economic policy and the wider macroeconomic environment;
Excellent analytical skills, better if with a background in economics, finance or tax;
Ability to conduct, analyse and present relevant research;
Strong writing and editing abilities. 

Communication:
Excellent interpersonal skills;
Proficiency in English speaking and writing ;
Efficiency in communicating with clients and team members;
Openness in sharing information and coordination. 

Teamwork:
Willing to learn from others and positively share ideas;
Working collaboratively with colleagues to achieve organizational goals.
